  "description": "In this report, we see how a sensitive information disclosure in a Gitea repository history exposed administrative credentials for Krayin CRM. This allowed authenticated remote code execution via CVE-2026-38526, granting initial access as www-data. Local enumeration then revealed a server-side configuration file with credentials that were reused for SSH access as the jones user. Finally, a directory traversal vulnerability in a root-executed Gitea template synchronization service was exploited by crafting malicious Git tree objects to write an SSH public key and escalate to root.",
